\paragraph{Concurrent work.}
\citet{landesberg2026bon} document an analogous correlation-selection gap in best-of-$N$ reasoning: global judge correlation $r{=}0.47$ masks within-prompt ranking $r{=}0.27$. While the mechanism differs---scoring granularity in LLM judging vs.\ entity-set degeneracy and LP compression in NER---the convergence of independent findings suggests the correlation-selection gap is a general phenomenon in sample-based inference, not NER-specific. Our contribution is the mechanistic diagnosis: identifying \emph{why} correlation fails to transfer.

\paragraph{What is new.}
We provide the first instance-level diagnostic framework for NER, extending beyond task-level analysis \cite{yao2026consistency}, qualitative failure modes \cite{chen2023twofailures}, and discrete-answer diversity \cite{yun2025price}.

